# Agent tooling and session-local state. Whole directories, not selected files.
#
# The July 2026 history rewrite removed .claude/handoff.md and .claude/standards.md from every
# commit: they carried a dead tunnel hostname, local absolute paths, references to a throwaway
# Postgres password and session notes. Only three subpaths under .claude/ were ignored, so those
# two files were one `git add -A` from returning to a public repository. .agents/ (943 files) was
# not ignored at all. Ignore the directories, so the decision is enforced rather than remembered.
.claude/
.agents/
.opencode/
.tmp/

# BMAD tooling installation (each developer installs locally via BMAD installer)
_bmad/

# Design corpus: planning and implementation artifacts, and any generated test artifacts.
#
# Removed from every commit by the July 2026 history rewrite, and that decision stands. The copy
# on disk is a working knowledge base, not repository content.
#
# What used to be here, and why it is gone: a rule excluded _bmad-output/test-artifacts/* while
# re-including test-artifacts/conformance/, on the reasoning that a published OIDF plan is
# permanently immutable and its bundles are irreplaceable certification evidence rather than
# regenerable output. That reasoning was right and the rule is now a dead letter — an exclusion of
# the whole directory means git cannot re-include anything inside it, and the bundles are in any
# case no longer on disk or in the history. The published results still live with the OIDF; the
# in-repo copies did not survive the rewrite. Do not restore the negation without first restoring
# the files and re-deciding whether they should be public.
_bmad-output/

# Local conformance run config (contains local Postgres credentials; docker template lives in tests/conformance/config)
src/RufistoWard.Host/appsettings.Conformance.json

